        "id": "0f9bb71e-6557-476e-94eb-fce5c7d41fe8",
        "name": "AllowedGrantTypes",
        "label": {
          "en": "Allowed Grant Types"
        },
        "description": {
          "en": "The grants this client may use. **Must not carry a non-empty initializer.**\nRavenDB's serializer populates the collection the property initializer already created rather than replacing it, so a default of [\"authorization_code\"] was silently re-added to every application on load. A client stored as client_credentials-only came back as [\"authorization_code\", \"client_credentials\"] — which defeats the grant gating outright: the interactive flow accepted a machine client no matter what was configured, and the check that was supposed to stop it could never fail.\nEmpty now means empty, so a client that declares no grants can use none — fail closed."
        },
        "dataType": "string",
        "isRequired": false,
        "isVisible": true,
        "isReadOnly": false,
        "order": 6,
        "isArray": true,
        "showedOn": "Query, PersistentObject",
