        "label": {
          "en": "May Introspect Any Audience"
        },
        "description": {
          "en": "Lets this client introspect tokens it neither issued nor is the audience of.\nOff by default: introspection discloses a token's subject and scopes, so the caller must have a reason to see them — it issued the token, or the token was minted for it. Turn this on only for a gateway that introspects on behalf of the resources behind it, and understand that it can then read every token in the system."
